An eight bank, pin diode selected, pre-selector is used to improve the intermodulation performance and to reduce  the possibility of  harmonics of the local oscillator mixing unwanted signals to the base band. A typical pre-selector filter is shown in fi
gure 2.
\par 
\par {\b 
\par POWER SUPPLIES AND FILTERS
\par }\tab 
The power supplies for the DSP 100 card are derived from the Computer Bus.  Only the plus 12 volts and negative 5 volts computer power supplies are used. The negative 5 volt supply is filtered with an LC network.  The plus twelve volt supply is filtered 
with an LC network for the 12 volt supply used by the DSP 100 card. A linear five volt regulator is used to derive a clean 5 volt supply for the digital circuits on the DSP 100 card.
\par \tab Both the Receive antenna input and Exciter output have been provided with the capablity of having a 12 Volt bias applied to them. These bias circuits are as show in fig 2.
